# Generated by the harness at run time. Both carry repo paths, timings and
# verdicts, and neither is an input to anything, so a clone must not track
# them. Previously ignored only via .git/info/exclude, which is local to one
# machine: a fresh clone would have offered them for commit.
.claude/harness-ledger.jsonl
.claude/optimise-cycle-report.md

# Python bytecode cache. test/destructive-git-guard.test.js's M3 allowlist
# parity check imports hooks/destructive-git-guard.py as a module (to read
# its GIT_ENV_ALLOWLIST constant as real data, not scraped source text),
# which makes CPython write this on every run.
hooks/__pycache__/
